  "page1": {
    "title": "Standing on My Own Two Feet",
    "subtitle": "Making your own choices and taking care of what comes next.",
    "body": "Every morning, Mina waited for her mom to wake her up. One day she decided to set her own alarm. She wanted to manage her time herself.\n\nLiving an independent life does not mean doing everything alone. It means making your own choices and taking responsibility for them. When you choose, you own the result.\n\nMina now packs her bag the night before. Sometimes she forgets a book and feels upset. But she learns from that mistake instead of blaming others.\n\nBeing independent also means <mark>standing on your own feet</mark>. You think about what is right and decide for yourself. You do not just follow friends because they say so.\n\nLittle choices grow into big confidence. Each task makes your inner strength stronger. Step by step, you guide your own life.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/venus/2026-07/09.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "A student setting her own alarm and packing her bag, learning to make choices and take charge."
  },
